The red curve has the same,

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:54.820
but the constituents of the green and blue

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:56.860
change dramatically to create that same curve.

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:57.700
And this is what you were saying.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:58.540
You were saying that,

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.740
Oh, this one's not different than zero.

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:03.980
But you see, it's not quite where it needs to be

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:04.820
for the data.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.540
It's close to the right peak, but it's not quite.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.700
So it needs this to kind of shift it where it needs to be.

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:12.340
Where here, it's nowhere near the right phase.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.180
And so it needs a bit more cosine

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:15.540
to help it get over there.

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:16.580
Because without both,

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:18.980
you can't have the peak and trough anywhere.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.380
You're very restricted.

