00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:57.980
Even, and since you should get the same F statistic,

00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:01.220
no matter which parameterization you pick.

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:03.140
You could do time minus six, time minus seven,

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:04.460
time minus nine, right?

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:05.860
It's just a scaling factor.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.260
It will change the individual beta parameters,

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:11.220
but the joint red curve will stay the same

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:13.300
'cause it's finding the same maximum.

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:16.620
So this value should be the same.

